    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22-a18">

                <pb facs="0100" n="42" xml:id="pg42"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 19.</seg></opener>
                <head>[General Orders No. 3.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Headquarters District of the Rio
                                Grande, <hi rendition="#italic">Brownsville,
                            Texas</hi>,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 18, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The Mexican authorities having officially notified the commanding general that
                    the Ranchero has been ordered to cease publishing any articles insulting to our
                    government, people, and army, it is hereby ordered that all officers and
                    soldiers of this command shall not allow any person on this bank to insult any
                    person on the other side of the Rio Grande.</p>
                <p>By order of Major General Weitzel:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. D. WHEELER, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Adjutant
                        General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
